# Build context exclusions.
#
# The Dockerfile copies only requirements.lock and kato/, but without this file
# the whole repository is still sent to the daemon as build context, and COPY
# kato/ sweeps in whatever the builder happens to have on disk. That shipped 164
# stale .pyc files into the v5.1.0 image -- bytecode from the builder's own
# Python, which the image's interpreter can never use -- plus empty directories
# left behind by deleted modules, which then resolve as namespace packages.

# Python bytecode and caches (the reason this file exists).
# NOTE: .dockerignore is NOT gitignore. Patterns match the whole path from the
# context root with Go filepath.Match semantics, so a bare `__pycache__` only
# matches one at the top level -- nested ones need the `**/` prefix.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*$py.class
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.coverage
htmlcov

# Virtual environments
**/venv
**/.venv
ENV
env

# Version control and CI
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.pre-commit-config.yaml

# Everything outside the build inputs
tests/
benchmarks/
docs/
planning-docs/
examples/
charts/
deployment/
archive/
logs/
scripts/
assets/
config/

# Local environment and editor state
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp

# Build and release artifacts
build
dist
**/*.egg-info
**/*.tar.gz

# Docs and metadata not needed to build the image
*.md
!README.md
